        "Residual category."@en,
        "The coded player category scheme and the counterparty role scheme share this word but not its position in the event: the first was coded for the export side, the second for the host side. The concepts are linked with skos:closeMatch and deliberately not with skos:exactMatch."@en,
        "빈번히 사용되면 어휘 확장을 검토해야 한다."@ko,
        "잔여 범주."@ko,
        "정의문은 codebook v1.0 의 것을 그대로 옮겼다 (registry/codebook_v1.0.csv)."@ko ;
    skos:topConceptOf prole: ;
    nuproc:justifyingCompetencyQuestion "CQ02" ;
    nuproc:status "codebook v1.0 v1.0-draft; observed_n=14; status=in_use" .

srole: a skos:ConceptScheme ;
    rdfs:label "Side Role"@en ;
    dcterms:source "ADR-0040 §4" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/nuproc/codebook>,
        <https://w3id.org/nuproc/core> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3id.org/nuproc/adr/ADR-0001>,
        <https://w3id.org/nuproc/adr/ADR-0036>,
        <https://w3id.org/nuproc/adr/ADR-0040> ;
    skos:definition "The vocabulary naming which side of a two-sided engagement a participation is on: the export side or the host side. It does not say who initiated the engagement."@en,
        "두 쪽으로 이루어진 관여에서 참여가 어느 쪽인지 가리키는 어휘 — 수출 측 · 발주 (현지) 측. 누가 주도했는지가 아니다."@ko ;
    skos:hasTopConcept srole:export_side,
        srole:host_side ;
    skos:prefLabel "Side Role"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "The NuProc source data already separate the export side (player) from the host side (counterparty), so every NuProc participation carries a side value. In sources that have no export and host side (such as the EC meeting register or UCDP) the side role does not apply and the side key names the side"@en,
        "NuProc 원자료는 수출 측 (player) 과 발주 측 (counterparty) 을 이미 분리해 담고 있다 — NuProc 자료에서는 모든 참여가 측 값을 갖는다. 수출 · 발주 측이 없는 원천 (EC 면담 등록부 · UCDP 등) 에서는 측 역할이 해당 없고 sideKey 가 쪽을 이름 짓는다 (ADR-0036 · ADR-0040 §4)."@ko ;
    nuproc:justifyingCompetencyQuestion "CQ02;CQ03" ;
    nuproc:ontocleanRigidity "~R anti-rigid with respect to the organization (the same organization stands on different sides in different engagements). For a participation it is a property of the side, not part of the side's identity"@en,
        "~R 반강성 — 조직에 대해 (같은 조직이 관여에 따라 다른 쪽에 선다). 참여에게는 쪽의 속성이지 쪽의 동일성의 일부가 아니다 (ADR-0036)"@ko .

eident: a skos:ConceptScheme ;
    rdfs:label "Engagement Identification Status"@en ;
    dcterms:source "evaluation/coding/v3.0/VALIDATION_PROTOCOL.md §2.5" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/nuproc/codebook>,
        <https://w3id.org/nuproc/core> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3id.org/nuproc/adr/ADR-0027>,
        <https://w3id.org/nuproc/adr/ADR-0040> ;
    skos:definition "The vocabulary that says what the identification of a reported engagement-event cluster with one real engagement rests on: the key of the clustering rule alone, a person's check, or a person's judgement that the cluster brings together two or more engagements. It is the state of the identification linking a cluster to an engagement, not a property of the cluster."@en,
        "보도 사건 군집이 실제 관여 하나를 보도한다는 식별이 무엇에 기대는지 가리키는 어휘 — 군집 규칙의 키뿐인가, 사람이 확인했는가, 사람이 둘 이상의 관여가 묶였다고 판단했는가. 군집의 성질이 아니라 군집과 관여를 잇는 식별의 상태다."@ko ;
    skos:hasTopConcept eident:key_based,
        eident:merged,
        eident:verified ;
    skos:prefLabel "Engagement Identification Status"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "The clustering rule can put different meetings of one month under the same key into one cluster (under-separation) and split one engagement spanning two months into two clusters (over-separation). This state addresses the former. Over-separation can be represented by letting two clusters point to the same engagement individual (reportsEngagement is not inverse-functional), but it was not checked in this version. In NuProc data, verified and merged follow a person's check: in the validation sample, verified when both coders answer 'one engagement' and merged when both answer 'two or more'; in the re-check of the provisional multi-role clusters, the first author's answer; key-based otherwise"@en,
        "군집 규칙은 같은 달 같은 키의 서로 다른 회의를 한 군집으로 묶을 수 있고 (과소 분리), 두 달에 걸친 한 관여를 두 군집으로 가를 수 있다 (과다 분리). 이 상태는 앞의 것을 다룬다. 과다 분리는 두 군집이 같은 관여 개체를 가리키게 하여 나타낼 수 있으나 (reportsEngagement 는 역함수적이지 않다) 이 판에서는 확인하지 않았다. NuProc 자료에서 verified · merged 는 사람의 확인을 따른다 — 검증 표본에서는 두 코더가 모두 '하나' 면 verified, 모두 '둘 이상' 이면 merged; 잠정 다역할 군집의 재확인에서는 제1저자의 답; 그 밖은 key_based"@ko ;
    nuproc:justifyingCompetencyQuestion "CQ18" ;
    nuproc:ontocleanRigidity "~R anti-rigid — for the cluster: it changes with a person's check, and the cluster remains the same cluster. It is not a property of the engagement"@en,
        "~R 반강성 — 군집에 대해: 사람의 확인에 따라 바뀌고, 바뀌어도 같은 군집이다. 관여의 속성이 아니다"@ko .

tcstat: a skos:ConceptScheme ;
    rdfs:label "Type Classification Status"@en ;
    dcterms:source "docs/adr/ADR-0025-organization-type-axes.md" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/nuproc/codebook>,
        <https://w3id.org/nuproc/core> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3id.org/nuproc/adr/ADR-0025> ;
    skos:definition "The vocabulary of classification states for assigning an organization type. It records the researcher's evidential state, not a property of the organization."@en,
        "조직 유형 부여의 분류 상태 어휘. 유형을 판정할 근거가 있는지에 대한 연구자의 상태이지 조직의 성질이 아니다."@ko ;
    skos:hasTopConcept tcstat:confirmed,
        tcstat:disputed,
        tcstat:undetermined ;
    skos:prefLabel "Type Classification Status"@en ;
    nuproc:justifyingCompetencyQuestion "CQ02" ;
    nuproc:ontocleanRigidity "~R anti-rigid — with respect to the researcher's assignment: it changes once evidence is secured. Not a property of the organization"@en,
        "~R 반강성 — 연구자의 부여에 대해: 근거가 확보되면 바뀐다. 조직의 속성이 아니다"@ko .

channel: a skos:ConceptScheme ;
    rdfs:label "Engagement Channel"@en ;
    dcterms:source "codebook activity_type"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/nuproc/codebook>,
        <https://w3id.org/nuproc/core> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3id.org/nuproc/adr/ADR-0005>,
        <https://w3id.org/nuproc/adr/ADR-0018> ;
    skos:definition "The channel vocabulary that distinguishes engagement activities by the kinds of party on the export side and the host side (G2G / B2G / B2B)."@en,
        "관여 활동을 주체와 상대의 조합으로 구분하는 채널 어휘 (G2G / B2G / B2B)."@ko ;
    skos:hasTopConcept channel:B2B,
        channel:B2G,
        channel:G2G,
        channel:Unknown ;
    skos:prefLabel "Engagement Channel"@en ;
    nuproc:justifyingCompetencyQuestion "CQ01;CQ09;CQ10" ;
    nuproc:ontocleanRigidity "It is not a property of an organization. For EngagementCluster this value is one element of the identity key — it is essential to the cluster (ADR-0032 §3)"@en,
        "조직의 속성이 아니다. EngagementCluster 에게 이 값은 동일성 키의 한 요소다 — 군집에 본질적이다 (ADR-0032 §3)"@ko .

ostat: a skos:ConceptScheme ;
    rdfs:label "Occurrence Status"@en ;
    dcterms:source "registry/codebook_occurrence_v1.csv; evaluation/coding/occurrence_v1/CODING_PROTOCOL.md §2"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/nuproc/codebook>,
        <https://w3id.org/nuproc/core> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3id.org/nuproc/adr/ADR-0041> ;
    skos:definition "The vocabulary that says whether the engagement reported by the records of an engagement-event cluster had taken place, or was under way, when it was reported: occurred, planned, denied or unclear. It is a value coded about the reported engagement, not a property of the engagement, and not an occurrence confirmed from sources other than the articles."@en,
        "보도 사건 군집의 기록들이 보도하는 관여가, 보도된 시점에, 일어났거나 진행 중이었는지 가리키는 어휘 — 일어남 · 예정 · 부인 · 불명. 관여의 성질이 아니라 보도된 관여에 대해 코딩된 값이다 — 기사 밖의 자료로 확인한 발생이 아니다."@ko ;
    skos:hasTopConcept ostat:denied,
        ostat:occurred,
        ostat:planned,
        ostat:unclear ;
    skos:prefLabel "Occurrence Status"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "The definitions and the inclusion and exclusion rules of the four values are those of the codebook codebook_occurrence_v1, frozen before coding, and of its coding protocol. The status is separate from the identification status: verified is a person's confirmation that the records report one engagement, not that the engagement took place. An engagement is asserted in the real-world layer only for a cluster whose final occurrence status is occurred and that is not merged"@en,
        "네 값의 정의 · 포함 · 제외 규칙은 코딩 전에 동결한 코드북 codebook_occurrence_v1 과 그 코딩 규약 §2 다. 식별 상태와 따로다 — verified 는 기록들이 관여 하나를 보도한다는 사람의 확인이지 그 관여가 일어났다는 확인이 아니다. 실세계 층의 관여는 최종 발생 상태가 occurred 이고 병합되지 않은 군집에만 단언한다 (ADR-0041 §2)"@ko ;
    nuproc:justifyingCompetencyQuestion "CQ18;CQ20" ;
    nuproc:ontocleanRigidity "~R anti-rigid for a cluster: it changes with coding and the human check, and the cluster stays the same cluster when it changes. It is not a property of the engagement"@en,
        "~R 반강성 — 군집에 대해: 코딩 · 사람 점검에 따라 바뀌고, 바뀌어도 같은 군집이다. 관여의 속성이 아니다"@ko .

otype: a skos:ConceptScheme ;
    rdfs:label "Organization Type"@en ;
    dcterms:source "docs/adr/ADR-0014-two-role-axes.md (decision A); actor_type in the source dataset's coding manual (not distributed)"@en,
        "ADR-0014 결정 A; 매뉴얼 actor_type"@ko ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/nuproc/codebook>,
        <https://w3id.org/nuproc/core> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3id.org/nuproc/adr/ADR-0014>,
        <https://w3id.org/nuproc/adr/ADR-0021>,
        <https://w3id.org/nuproc/adr/ADR-0025> ;
    skos:definition "The vocabulary of fixed organization types, such as government body, state-owned enterprise or private firm. It is not a coding output but a value the researcher fixes; the value list and the assignment were fixed in the actor registry and filled in v0.2."@en,
        "조직의 고정 유형 어휘 (예: 정부기관 / 국유기업 / 민간기업). 코딩 산출물이 아니라 연구자가 확정하는 값이다 — 값 목록과 부여를 행위자 레지스트리에서 확정해 v0.2 에 채웠다."@ko ;
    skos:editorialNote "This scheme was deliberately left empty in v0.1 and filled in v0.2 from the actor registry, where the researcher fixed both the value list and the assignment. Coded player_role values are never promoted into it: in the source dataset's actor labels, five carry two or more player_role values and cover 71.4% (733/1,026) of the design events, so the coded value is an event-level role, not a fixed organization type. The entity_overrides table of the source dataset's coding manual (not distributed) is not the source either: its keys name the same axis as player_role, so reading a type off it would be that same promotion."@en ;
    skos:hasTopConcept otype:Government,
        otype:PrivateFirm,
        otype:Public,
        otype:SOE ;
    skos:prefLabel "Organization Type"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Left deliberately empty in v0.1 and filled from the actor registry in v0.2."@en,
        "v0.1 에서는 의도적으로 비워 두었고 v0.2 에서 행위자 레지스트리로 채웠다 (ADR-0021)."@ko ;
    nuproc:justifyingCompetencyQuestion "CQ02" ;
    nuproc:ontocleanRigidity "-R non-rigid — essential to a government body but not to a state-owned enterprise or private firm (privatisation). That 0 organizations changed type in the observation period is an empirical fact, not a rigidity value (ADR-0025 revision · ADR-0032 §3)"@en,
        "-R 비강성 — 정부 기관에게는 본질적이지만 공기업·민간기업에게는 아니다(민영화). 관측 구간에서 유형이 바뀐 조직 0건은 강성 값이 아니라 경험적 사실이다 (ADR-0025 개정 · ADR-0032 §3)"@ko .

rstat: a skos:ConceptScheme ;
    rdfs:label "Resolution Status"@en ;
    dcterms:source "docs/adr/ADR-0008-unnamed-actor-reference.md; docs/adr/ADR-0010-khnp-kepco-merge.md (4-way classification)"@en,
        "ADR-0008;ADR-0010 4분류"@ko ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/nuproc/codebook>,
        <https://w3id.org/nuproc/core> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3id.org/nuproc/adr/ADR-0010> ;
    skos:definition "The vocabulary of resolution states for participant references. It structurally separates a failure to resolve from an impossibility of resolving."@en,
        "참여자 지칭의 해소 상태 어휘. 해소 실패와 해소 불가를 구조적으로 분리한다."@ko ;
    skos:hasTopConcept rstat:resolved,
        rstat:unresolvable_candidate_set,
        rstat:unresolvable_collective,
        rstat:unresolved ;
    skos:prefLabel "Resolution Status"@en ;
    nuproc:justifyingCompetencyQuestion "CQ17" ;
    nuproc:ontocleanRigidity "Anti-rigid (~R) for the unresolved and resolved values of a definite reference: they change according to decisions, and the reference is the same reference after it changes (ADR-0031 §3). The two unresolvable values are fixed by the kind of the reference (ReferenceKindStatusShape), so they do not change for that reference. Not a property of the organization"@en,
        "확정 지칭의 unresolved · resolved 는 ~R 반강성 — 결정에 따라 바뀌고, 바뀌어도 같은 지칭이다 (ADR-0031 §3). unresolvable_candidate_set · unresolvable_collective 는 지칭의 종류가 정하는 값이라 그 지칭에 고정된다 (ReferenceKindStatusShape). 조직의 속성이 아니다"@ko .

erole: a skos:ConceptScheme ;
    rdfs:label "Engagement Role Type"@en ;
    dcterms:source "codebook v3.0 engagement_role" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/nuproc/codebook>,
        <https://w3id.org/nuproc/core> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3id.org/nuproc/adr/ADR-0024>,
        <https://w3id.org/nuproc/adr/ADR-0040> ;
    skos:definition "The vocabulary of engagement role types that the export-side participant of an event has in the engagement the event reports, whether or not that engagement took place. The role types are facets: several may be coded for one participation. It carries no ownership or control character; that is carried by OrganizationType. Each value has a role class in the real-world layer (nuproc:roleClass)."@en,
        "사건의 수출 측 참여자가 그 사건이 보도한 관여에서 지니는 관여 역할 유형 어휘 (그 관여가 일어났는지와 무관하다). 다면 (facet) 이다 — 한 참여에 여럿이 함께 코딩될 수 있다. 소유 · 지배 성격을 담지 않는다 — 그것은 OrganizationType 이 진다. 값마다 실세계 층의 역할 클래스가 있다 (nuproc:roleClass)."@ko ;
    skos:hasTopConcept erole:commercial_supply,
        erole:construction_contract,
        erole:financing,
        erole:other,
        erole:state_sponsorship,
        erole:technology_supply ;
    skos:prefLabel "Engagement Role Type"@en ;
    nuproc:justifyingCompetencyQuestion "CQ02;CQ18" ;
    nuproc:ontocleanRigidity "~R anti-rigid with respect to the organization that takes the role (the same organization takes different roles in different engagements). For a participation it is a fixed coded value"@en,
        "~R 반강성 — 그 역할을 맡는 조직에 대해 (같은 조직이 관여에 따라 다른 역할을 맡는다). 참여에게는 고정된 코딩 값이다"@ko .

prole: a skos:ConceptScheme ;
    rdfs:label "Coded Player Category"@en ;
    dcterms:source "registry/codebook_v1.0.csv (player_role); in the source dataset's actor labels, 5 carry 2 or more categories and cover 71.4% of the design events"@en,
        "codebook player_role; ADR-0014 (원자료 행위자 표기 다섯이 2종 이상, 설계 사건의 71.4%)"@ko ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/nuproc/codebook>,
        <https://w3id.org/nuproc/core> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3id.org/nuproc/adr/ADR-0014>,
        <https://w3id.org/nuproc/adr/ADR-0024> ;
    skos:definition "The vocabulary of categories coded for the export-side participation. It is not a pure role vocabulary: three of its six values were assigned by an organization lookup. The engagement roles coded for the participant are carried by EngagementRoleType."@en,
        "수출 측 참여에 코딩된 범주 어휘. 순수 역할 어휘가 아니다 — 여섯 값 중 셋은 조직 조회로 부여됐다. 참여자에게 코딩된 관여 역할은 EngagementRoleType 이 담는다."@ko ;
    skos:hasTopConcept prole:epc_contractor,
        prole:government,
        prole:investor,
        prole:other,
        prole:private_firm,
        prole:soe_vendor ;
    skos:prefLabel "Coded Player Category"@en ;
    nuproc:justifyingCompetencyQuestion "CQ02;CQ09" ;
    nuproc:ontocleanRigidity "~R anti-rigid — with respect to the organization that has the value (Westinghouse is still Westinghouse when it ceases to be epc_contractor). For a participation it is a fixed coded value"@en,
        "~R 반강성 — 그 값을 갖는 조직에 대해 (Westinghouse 는 epc_contractor 이기를 그쳐도 Westinghouse 다). 참여에게는 고정된 코딩 값이다"@ko .

crole: a skos:ConceptScheme ;
    rdfs:label "Counterparty Role"@en ;
    dcterms:source "registry/codebook_v1.0.csv (counterparty_role)" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/nuproc/codebook>,
        <https://w3id.org/nuproc/core> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3id.org/nuproc/adr/ADR-0006>,
        <https://w3id.org/nuproc/adr/ADR-0014> ;
    skos:definition "The vocabulary of functional roles coded for the counterparty side of an event: what the counterparty did there. Authority is determined by function, not by ownership."@en,
        "사건의 상대측에 코딩된 기능 역할 어휘 — 상대측이 거기서 한 일. 권한은 소유가 아니라 기능으로 판정한다."@ko ;
    skos:hasTopConcept crole:epc_contractor,
        crole:host_firm,
        crole:host_government,
        crole:host_utility,
        crole:investor,
        crole:other,
        crole:project_owner_soe,
        crole:public_community,
        crole:regulator ;
    skos:prefLabel "Counterparty Role"@en ;
    nuproc:justifyingCompetencyQuestion "CQ03;CQ09;CQ11" ;
    nuproc:ontocleanRigidity "~R anti-rigid — with respect to the body that takes on the role (the same body is a gateway or a transaction counterparty depending on the event). For a participation it is a fixed coded value"@en,
        "~R 반강성 — 그 역할을 맡는 기관에 대해 (같은 기관이 사건에 따라 관문이거나 거래 상대다). 참여에게는 고정된 코딩 값이다"@ko .

etype: a skos:ConceptScheme ;
    rdfs:label "Event Type"@en ;
    dcterms:source "codebook primary_code"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/nuproc/codebook>,
        <https://w3id.org/nuproc/core> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3id.org/nuproc/adr/ADR-0005>,
        <https://w3id.org/nuproc/adr/ADR-0006> ;
    skos:definition "The vocabulary of engagement activity types (primary_code). Each notation except the residual Unknown carries the channel prefix."@en,
        "관여 활동의 유형 어휘 (primary_code). 잔여 값 Unknown 을 뺀 각 표기는 채널 접두사를 포함한다."@ko ;
    skos:hasTopConcept etype:B2B-1,
        etype:B2B-2,
        etype:B2B-3,
        etype:B2B-4,
        etype:B2B-Other,
        etype:B2G-1,
        etype:B2G-2,
        etype:B2G-3,
        etype:B2G-4,
        etype:B2G-Other,
        etype:G2G-1,
        etype:G2G-2,
        etype:G2G-3,
        etype:G2G-4,
        etype:G2G-5,
        etype:G2G-Other,
        etype:Unknown ;
    skos:prefLabel "Event Type"@en ;
    nuproc:justifyingCompetencyQuestion "CQ10;CQ11" ;
    nuproc:ontocleanRigidity "It is not a property of an organization. For EngagementCluster this value is one element of the identity key — it is essential to the cluster (ADR-0032 §3)"@en,
        "조직의 속성이 아니다. EngagementCluster 에게 이 값은 동일성 키의 한 요소다 — 군집에 본질적이다 (ADR-0032 §3)"@ko .

<https://w3id.org/nuproc/codebook> a owl:Ontology ;
    dcterms:creator "Wonbae Park" ;
    dcterms:description "The eleven SKOS concept schemes of NuProc: engagement channel, event type, coded player category, engagement role type, counterparty role, side role, organization type, type classification status, resolution status, engagement identification status and occurrence status. The values of the engagement role type and side role schemes are linked to the classes of the real-world roles they stand for (nuproc:roleClass)."@en ;
    dcterms:issued "2026-08-17"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-10-29"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:title "NuProc Ontology — codebook vocabularies"@en ;
    vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "nuproc" ;
    vann:preferredNamespaceUri "https://w3id.org/nuproc/ns#" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/bonjwanim/nuprockg> ;
    owl:imports <https://w3id.org/nuproc/core> ;
    owl:priorVersion <https://w3id.org/nuproc/codebook/0.8.0> ;
    owl:versionIRI <https://w3id.org/nuproc/codebook/0.9.0> ;
    owl:versionInfo "0.9.0" ;
    nuproc:status "v0.9.0 release. The licence is CC BY 4.0. This version is a logical revision of v0.8.0. It separates the identification of a reported cluster with one engagement from the occurrence of that engagement: a cluster carries a coded occurrence status (OccurrenceStatus: occurred, planned, denied or unclear) with one claim per coded value (OccurrenceClaim), and only a cluster whose occurrence status is occurred, and that a person has not judged to merge engagements, reports an engagement, as do its records. The axiom that every event record reports an engagement was removed, so that the report of a planned or denied engagement does not imply that the engagement exists. A group of organizations acting together as one party, such as a consortium, is one organization whose members are given with W3C ORG (org:hasMember), and the pattern layer again allows at most one participant organization per participation. Each judgement of how an actor reference is resolved is a claim (ResolutionClaim) with the status it gives and, for a resolved reference, the organization; the status and resolvedTo asserted on a reference are those of its final claim, and the claims that were not adopted remain. Each judgement of what a cluster's identification with one engagement rests on (the clustering key alone, a person's check, or a person's finding that it merges engagements) is likewise a claim (IdentificationClaim). A procurement case is aligned, like an engagement, to the BFO process. The information-layer property that names the organization a coded participation denotes is now namesParticipant (hasParticipant in v0.8.0), apart from RO's has participant. The SHACL pattern layer now also requires that a record whose cluster reports no engagement reports none, that an activity which made a final claim names its agent and plan on a qualified association, and that an engagement in the data is reported by a cluster, and it lets only a cluster whose occurrence status is occurred ground a role or a side role (a rule for asserting roles, not a condition of their existence). The disjointness axioms now also cover the occurrence, resolution and identification claims, codebook versions, prompt specifications, quality measurements and the clustering rule, and organizations, roles and cases, like engagements, are disjoint with the coding and validation activities. v0.8.0 added a real-world layer whose classes are aligned by IRI to BFO and whose relations are reused from RO and BFO: an engagement (Engagement) is a process in which parties engage with one another over a procurement case, organizations participate in it, and the engagement roles of an organization (EngagementRole, with two side roles and six role facets) are its roles in a procurement case and are realized in the engagements of that case in which it acts in them; clusters and records report engagements (reportsEngagement, a subproperty of IAO is about). It replaced the single coded engagement function with engagement role types that may be combined, with one claim per coded value (RoleClaim), and the direction role with a side role, and added class restrictions, a functional property, disjointness axioms and the pattern-layer constraints on role claims, qualified associations and the real-world layer. No aliases are kept for renamed terms, because no earlier version was released. v0.7.0 renamed the information entities (EngagementCluster, CodedParticipation, concernsCase), added the function claims and the IAO alignment, and corrected two pattern-layer constraints on actor references. v0.6.1 revised annotations only. v0.6.0 made the direction role optional in the SHACL pattern layer and added the side key; that revision was designed after the v0.5.0 cross-dataset reuse results had been seen. The earlier logical revisions were v0.5.0 (reference resolution completed, coding plans, and SHACL shapes split into a domain-neutral pattern layer and a NuProc profile layer), v0.4.0 (a counterparty participation may carry one participant) and v0.3.0 (the player axis split into a coded category and an engagement function, organization-type axes, typed actor references, and the event as an analytical cluster). No earlier version was released. The cross-dataset reuse results and the reserved-case results reported with this version were obtained on it. No ORCID identifier is recorded for the creator."@en .

